      "value": "@{64873f159cf028090ce2c2e2|full_name} - I can confirm that this issue is still present. I tested and confirmed it today in desktop and VR mode. \n\nHere's another report about the same issue: \n\nhttps://feedback.vrchat.com/bug-reports/p/1144-crouch-walking-up-an-inclineslope-causes-step-stuttering \n\n(Although that report mistakenly implies that it only occurs when crouching.) \n\nIn my experience, this issue occurs when moving up the majority of gentle slopes. While testing again today, I discovered an interesting case where the issue doesn't occur, which might help the engineers debug this. Here's a video demonstration: \n\nhttps://youtu.be/XKMUAhKiJbg",
