  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "VRChat build: 1149\nWhen moving up slopes, the view does not smoothly move up, but instead moves up in discrete steps like when walking up a mesh collider shaped like a staircase. This is particularly noticeable in VR.\nTo reproduce:\n1. Go to the wall with the night/daytime options in the VRChat Home world and climb on top\n2. Move up the slope slowly (in desktop, use prone)\n3. Notice stair-like vertical movement\nThis only happens when moving up slopes, and not down. Some of the slopes in the VRChat Home (like the one near spawn) do not exhibit this behavior - maybe this only affects mesh colliders and not rotated box colliders.",
